00:38:33.420 --> 00:38:38.560
they were there i feel like the game in general was a little more kind to people who not necessarily

00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:43.440
were like willing to explore there's nothing there's no like hidden uh canals or anything but

00:38:43.440 --> 00:38:49.760
like more willing to um to spend time with it and and know about these these things the unfortunate

00:38:49.760 --> 00:38:55.560
thing is is again if you die while having none of this stuff there isn't like oh well i'll just go

00:38:55.560 --> 00:39:00.980
back to this other stage where i know there's plenty of ammo refills and refill up before i take on the new

00:39:00.980 --> 00:39:03.760
stage you know you can't do that you can't go backwards

00:39:03.760 --> 00:39:04.940
you

00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:05.900
qu'

00:40:07.320 --> 00:40:08.140
qu'

00:40:08.140 --> 00:40:10.160
qu' qu'

00:40:11.100 --> 00:40:11.920
qu'

00:40:11.920 --> 00:40:13.360
qu'

00:40:23.940 --> 00:40:28.880
I don't know about you guys, but that bee who drops down those five bees,

00:40:29.140 --> 00:40:31.040
that is nightmare stuff right now.

00:40:31.040 --> 00:40:33.980
That's the first enemy I ran into and really like,

00:40:34.080 --> 00:40:35.780
oh, this is going to be a fun time.

00:40:36.160 --> 00:40:40.780
Then you got the one on the pogo stick or plunger or whatever.

00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:42.640
Yeah, yeah. He does like a pole vault.

00:40:42.960 --> 00:40:49.880
And you have to do this very specific dodge move just to –

00:40:49.880 --> 00:40:54.200
because you can't hit him from the front until – I don't know.

00:40:54.480 --> 00:40:55.780
Yeah, until after he vaults.

00:40:55.900 --> 00:40:59.020
And then you have to – basically you have to slide under his vault

00:40:59.020 --> 00:41:03.080
and then let him run at you, jump over him,

00:41:03.100 --> 00:41:06.420
and then shoot him like three times in order to take him out.

00:41:06.440 --> 00:41:07.460
And that's just one time.

00:41:07.660 --> 00:41:08.740
That's one enemy.

00:41:08.900 --> 00:41:11.780
It's not like you're going to, oh, good, I'm glad I got him out of the way.

00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:14.420
He's going to do that three more times on that very screen.

00:41:15.240 --> 00:41:20.740
Yeah, I feel this way about I think all three of the Mega Man games,

00:41:20.840 --> 00:41:24.480
but there are a lot of enemies in them that you need to understand

00:41:24.480 --> 00:41:28.800
the pattern that they're going – like their flight path or whatever

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:31.780
before they come at you in order to dodge them.

00:41:31.860 --> 00:41:32.820
You can't react.

00:41:32.980 --> 00:41:34.880
You have to preemptively react.

00:41:35.080 --> 00:41:36.680
Where there are things like on the ceiling,

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:37.900
I'm like, this is going to swoop down at me,

00:41:37.980 --> 00:41:40.700
but it swoops down in a trajectory where it's like,

00:41:40.740 --> 00:41:42.340
well, I couldn't have predicted that,

00:41:42.340 --> 00:41:46.740
and it seemed to predict kind of where I was going to go in a way

00:41:46.740 --> 00:41:49.100
where it's like I needed to know it was going to do that beforehand.

00:41:49.720 --> 00:41:51.720
I almost feel like I can't just dodge.

00:41:51.840 --> 00:41:53.180
The bees were one of them.

00:41:53.500 --> 00:41:56.020
Maybe not even that exact circumstance,

00:41:56.580 --> 00:41:59.240
but the bees, even the speed runners I'm watching

00:41:59.240 --> 00:42:00.320
are getting hit by the bees.

00:42:00.780 --> 00:42:03.160
I just feel like you can't dodge those bees.

00:42:03.360 --> 00:42:04.620
Well, on that note,

00:42:06.200 --> 00:42:10.060
I think a lot of times the most efficient way to move forward

00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:12.100
is just to take a hit or two.

00:42:12.100 --> 00:42:13.320
There is knockback,

00:42:13.420 --> 00:42:16.720
but it's not like a guarantee to throw you down.

00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:18.640
It's not Castlevania knockback, yeah.

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:21.020
Yeah, and it's not always a guarantee

00:42:21.020 --> 00:42:23.700
that even if you are on kind of like a small platform

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:24.880
that you're going to fall,

00:42:26.420 --> 00:42:29.900
it's still very likely that you're going to fall from that knockback

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:32.840
and lose a life and go all the way back.

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:36.780
But if you are smart with it,

00:42:36.980 --> 00:42:37.880
you can, like,

00:42:37.960 --> 00:42:40.960
that is I think a valid strategy is just take the hit.

00:42:40.960 --> 00:42:41.780
Mm-hmm.

00:42:42.260 --> 00:42:44.660
And the bees, sorry to stay on them,

00:42:44.780 --> 00:42:48.540
but, like, it does feel like there's one singular bee

00:42:48.540 --> 00:42:51.320
that drops, like, what, a bunch of larva eggs or something?

00:42:51.340 --> 00:42:52.680
Is that what he's holding?

00:42:52.900 --> 00:42:54.840
Yeah. And then they break free from that.

00:42:55.140 --> 00:42:57.100
It does feel like there should be a moment

00:42:57.100 --> 00:42:58.800
where it's like, oh, not a big deal.

00:42:59.020 --> 00:43:03.220
I'll shoot the larva before it touches the platform

00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:06.040
and breaks open so that I have to deal with five bees.

00:43:06.040 --> 00:43:08.020
You cannot do that, for the record.

00:43:08.240 --> 00:43:10.560
Don't, I tried a lot of, even with emulation,

00:43:10.780 --> 00:43:12.260
like, rewinding and being perfect.

00:43:12.420 --> 00:43:13.700
It does not happen.

00:43:13.900 --> 00:43:16.480
The bees will come out

00:43:16.480 --> 00:43:18.760
and you'll have to deal with all five of them.

00:43:19.240 --> 00:43:21.880
And I feel like there are other enemies in this game

00:43:21.880 --> 00:43:24.720
that fly and come at you, like those penguins,

00:43:24.880 --> 00:43:26.600
but, like, they were much more manageable

00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:28.240
than the bees were.

00:43:28.240 --> 00:43:29.740
So the bees are just, like,

00:43:29.880 --> 00:43:34.240
it's really just because there's a lot of spike deaths

00:43:34.240 --> 00:43:37.260
and, or endless platforms and stuff like that.

00:43:37.320 --> 00:43:38.600
So it becomes harder.

00:43:39.020 --> 00:43:40.340
It's, again, I think to Sean's point,

00:43:40.500 --> 00:43:43.760
just tank the hit and move on and it's fine.

00:43:43.960 --> 00:43:44.920
Like, they won't be able to chase you

00:43:44.920 --> 00:43:46.040
through the entirety of the stage,

00:43:46.040 --> 00:43:48.260
but it also, like, slows down the game tremendously.

00:43:48.260 --> 00:43:50.060
So it has that going for it in terms of, like,

00:43:50.120 --> 00:43:52.060
being on time and jumping over them.

00:43:52.080 --> 00:43:55.400
There was some terrible, some terrible slowdown.

00:43:55.400 --> 00:43:58.360
Overall, though, like, the Mega Man world,

00:43:58.560 --> 00:44:00.820
I know we established that there's no central government

00:44:00.820 --> 00:44:04.700
or anything, but, like, the enemies and characters,

00:44:04.980 --> 00:44:09.400
like, for the same reasons people love Final Fantasy

00:44:09.400 --> 00:44:13.880
or Dragon Quest, like, and the enemies you see in those games,

00:44:13.920 --> 00:44:16.520
like, I am starting to appreciate the charm

00:44:16.520 --> 00:44:17.700
of the Mega Man world,

00:44:17.900 --> 00:44:20.400
not just with the new characters we meet

00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:22.880
that become main characters, like Rush and Proto Man,

00:44:22.880 --> 00:44:26.840
but, like, those guys who wear the hard hats

00:44:26.840 --> 00:44:28.840
and look like Goombas almost, you know,

00:44:28.960 --> 00:44:32.100
because they're so small, like, they amuse me now.

00:44:32.180 --> 00:44:34.020
They're like the Mega Man world minions.

00:44:35.540 --> 00:44:36.900
Yeah, they're cute.

00:44:36.980 --> 00:44:40.720
They're cute. I think that we're not at the point yet

00:44:40.720 --> 00:44:43.340
where it is, like, self-parody,

00:44:43.340 --> 00:44:49.100
but once we get to our place in time,

00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:51.320
like, I think that the Mega Man,

00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:53.300
like, other mans,

00:44:53.760 --> 00:44:55.780
like, the, like, Top Man is already

00:44:55.780 --> 00:44:57.240
kind of getting close to, like, this.

00:44:57.360 --> 00:44:58.540
What do you mean, Top Man?

00:44:58.720 --> 00:45:00.100
Yeah, yeah, where's Bottom Man?

00:45:02.320 --> 00:45:03.780
I don't even mean, like,

00:45:03.800 --> 00:45:08.240
in any kind of euphemistic way.

00:45:08.400 --> 00:45:10.800
It's just, like, you were getting into really

00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:12.640
silly things. Yeah, you've run out of, like, elements

00:45:12.640 --> 00:45:16.380
and you're onto, like, toy, like,

00:45:16.720 --> 00:45:19.300
mini toys. It should be mentioned that the,

00:45:19.560 --> 00:45:20.940
just like in Mega Man 2,

00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:23.540
the robots here were designed

00:45:23.540 --> 00:45:24.780
as part of a contest

00:45:24.780 --> 00:45:26.900
that Capcom held

00:45:26.900 --> 00:45:28.740
for fans in Japan,

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:30.600
and there was apparently over

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:32.360
50,000 submissions

00:45:32.360 --> 00:45:34.860
for ideas for the Robot Masters,

00:45:35.100 --> 00:45:37.520
and, yes, somehow Top Man won

00:45:37.520 --> 00:45:39.520
as one of those designs.

00:45:40.440 --> 00:45:41.600
I don't know, like,

00:45:41.760 --> 00:45:43.320
what you got as the grand prize

00:45:43.320 --> 00:45:45.000
for being one of the selected things.

00:45:45.040 --> 00:45:45.920
It is kind of amazing

00:45:45.920 --> 00:45:47.000
that a company was able

00:45:47.000 --> 00:45:49.440
to just, like, freelance its workout

00:45:49.440 --> 00:45:50.580
for free

00:45:51.160 --> 00:45:52.260
to a bunch of kids

00:45:52.260 --> 00:45:53.280
to, like, come, I don't know,

00:45:53.320 --> 00:45:54.520
you guys come up with the robots,

00:45:54.540 --> 00:45:55.400
and they did it.

00:45:55.700 --> 00:45:57.020
But I did find,

00:45:57.240 --> 00:45:58.040
oddly enough, there was, like,

00:45:58.060 --> 00:45:59.100
an eBay auction

00:45:59.600 --> 00:46:00.700
maybe back in, like,

00:46:01.600 --> 00:46:02.700
I don't know, the 2010s.

00:46:02.740 --> 00:46:03.760
I didn't even check the exact date,

00:46:03.820 --> 00:46:04.660
but it looks pretty old

00:46:04.660 --> 00:46:06.640
and expired of a guy

00:46:06.640 --> 00:46:07.540
who sold

00:46:07.540 --> 00:46:10.780
his runner-up

00:46:11.380 --> 00:46:12.260
pencil tin

00:46:12.260 --> 00:46:14.160
and ID card

00:46:14.160 --> 00:46:15.520
