00:46:15.520 --> 00:46:17.600
as, like, your design wasn't selected,

00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:18.700
but you're awesome,

00:46:19.220 --> 00:46:20.360
and we love your idea,

00:46:20.560 --> 00:46:22.620
so we gave you

00:46:22.620 --> 00:46:23.440
an ID card

00:46:23.440 --> 00:46:24.880
and a pencil tin,

00:46:25.460 --> 00:46:26.500
and unfortunately...

00:46:26.500 --> 00:46:27.480
What is the ID card?

00:46:27.760 --> 00:46:29.420
The ID card is in Japanese,

00:46:29.540 --> 00:46:30.840
so I don't know exactly what it says,

00:46:30.980 --> 00:46:32.100
but oddly enough...

00:46:32.100 --> 00:46:33.720
Does it grant you entry to Capcom?

00:46:34.020 --> 00:46:34.820
No, it doesn't,

00:46:34.860 --> 00:46:35.880
but here's something interesting.

00:46:36.900 --> 00:46:38.240
So it's an ID card,

00:46:38.260 --> 00:46:39.220
and you designed

00:46:39.220 --> 00:46:40.500
a robot master,

00:46:40.540 --> 00:46:41.460
so, of course,

00:46:41.640 --> 00:46:43.020
who would be,

00:46:43.020 --> 00:46:44.920
like, who would be authorizing you?

00:46:45.440 --> 00:46:47.020
Yeah, you're Dr. Wily.

00:46:47.180 --> 00:46:48.960
You're one of his... Dr. Wily, yes, exactly.

00:46:49.340 --> 00:46:50.200
You're his minions.

00:46:50.560 --> 00:46:51.760
Yeah, the bad guy here

00:46:51.760 --> 00:46:52.600
is thanking you

00:46:52.600 --> 00:46:53.620
for helping him

00:46:53.620 --> 00:46:55.500
create another robot master

00:46:55.500 --> 00:46:57.040
to take down Mega Man.

00:46:57.580 --> 00:46:58.600
Cute, though,

00:46:58.780 --> 00:47:00.340
Mega Man is on the...

00:47:00.340 --> 00:47:01.700
Even the guy saved the envelope.

00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:03.260
That it came in in the mail,

00:47:03.380 --> 00:47:05.180
and Mega Man is on the envelope

00:47:05.180 --> 00:47:06.080
along with Capcom

00:47:06.080 --> 00:47:06.920
and their official address

00:47:06.920 --> 00:47:08.880
and everything, so it's kind of sad

00:47:08.880 --> 00:47:11.520
that, like, Capcom won't revisit,

00:47:11.540 --> 00:47:13.340
like, who is basically their mascot

00:47:13.340 --> 00:47:14.360
at this point in time.

00:47:14.500 --> 00:47:15.820
Like, they won't revisit this guy,

00:47:15.900 --> 00:47:17.520
but they're happy to just keep churning out

00:47:17.520 --> 00:47:18.480
Monster Hunter games,

00:47:18.540 --> 00:47:20.160
which don't interest me at all,

00:47:20.220 --> 00:47:21.540
but clearly make a lot of money

00:47:21.540 --> 00:47:24.340
for the company. You know,

00:47:24.440 --> 00:47:25.860
or, like, I don't know, Sean,

00:47:26.160 --> 00:47:26.980
Resident Evil, like,

00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:27.820
is Leon,

00:47:28.080 --> 00:47:30.160
like, the main person

00:47:30.160 --> 00:47:31.840
that should be the mascot of Capcom,

00:47:31.840 --> 00:47:32.900
or is that, like, no?

00:47:33.520 --> 00:47:36.060
I mean, I don't have the same...

00:47:36.060 --> 00:47:37.220
I don't have the same problem

00:47:37.220 --> 00:47:38.260
because I don't have

00:47:38.260 --> 00:47:41.320
any kind of emotional connection

00:47:41.320 --> 00:47:42.640
to Mega Man,

00:47:43.920 --> 00:47:44.820
and I do

00:47:44.820 --> 00:47:45.940
with Resident Evil,

00:47:46.060 --> 00:47:47.720
so I'm pretty okay with it.

00:47:47.780 --> 00:47:49.380
I also don't care about

00:47:49.380 --> 00:47:50.620
Monster Hunter, though.

00:47:50.620 --> 00:47:52.580
But I guess which Resident Evil

00:47:52.580 --> 00:47:54.920
person should be, like,

00:47:55.020 --> 00:47:57.420
the mascot? Obviously,

00:47:57.720 --> 00:47:58.600
hyper-buff

00:47:58.600 --> 00:47:59.620
Chris Redfield

00:47:59.620 --> 00:48:01.000
with biceps

00:48:01.000 --> 00:48:02.680
larger than his head.

00:48:02.880 --> 00:48:03.920
Let it be written...

00:48:03.920 --> 00:48:05.600
Biceps larger than twice his head.

00:48:05.600 --> 00:48:06.860
Sorry to interrupt

00:48:06.860 --> 00:48:21.380
Sorry to interrupt

00:48:21.700 --> 00:48:30.500
Sorry to interrupt!

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:31.880
Sorry to interrupt!!

00:48:38.020 --> 00:48:40.900
So, you know, just real fast, because we're talking about the contest.

00:48:41.440 --> 00:48:51.060
Top Man, obviously, is the funny one, but Shadow Man, Spark Man, Magnet Man, Hard Man, Gemini Man, Needle Man, Snake Man.

00:48:51.700 --> 00:49:03.400
You know, I feel like for what it's worth, I understand that a competition that receives 50,000 submissions generates a lot of great buzz for Capcom and potential sales and everything.

00:49:03.400 --> 00:49:09.000
But Capcom totally could have also just came up with these same villains, right?

00:49:09.140 --> 00:49:17.160
Like, it didn't require the masses to be like, we're out of ideas, we need your help.

00:49:17.260 --> 00:49:19.660
Like, to our point, it's the third Mega Man game.

00:49:19.800 --> 00:49:21.540
You still have elements you can use.

00:49:21.540 --> 00:49:25.500
You have, like, you know, there's an endless, we know it.

00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:28.020
There's up to 10 Mega Mans and all those Mega Man X games.

00:49:28.140 --> 00:49:29.060
Like, we know there are others.

00:49:29.400 --> 00:49:33.320
But here, they're already asking for help.

00:49:33.760 --> 00:49:38.740
Yeah, there is something very alluring to me about the idea of, like, being a kid.

00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:46.280
And, you know, games that I liked, I would design my own games, like, on a piece of paper with colored pencils, you know?

00:49:46.420 --> 00:49:52.400
So the idea that, like, just the imagination involved in, like, oh, like, people just made these.

00:49:52.540 --> 00:49:56.740
Like, you can make a Mega Man, what are they called?

00:49:57.320 --> 00:49:58.560
Bad Robot Master.

00:49:59.040 --> 00:50:01.280
Yeah. No, what are these enemies called?

00:50:01.560 --> 00:50:02.820
The Robot Masters.

00:50:03.060 --> 00:50:06.560
You can make a Robot Master, like, out of anything you can think of.

00:50:06.640 --> 00:50:08.160
Like, that's just cool to me.

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:10.560
You know, yeah, obviously you're right.

00:50:10.660 --> 00:50:11.820
Like, they didn't need to do this.

00:50:11.820 --> 00:50:13.040
But I think you said it.

00:50:13.160 --> 00:50:14.060
It's a PR thing.

00:50:14.180 --> 00:50:18.300
And it seems to have been effective.

00:50:18.620 --> 00:50:23.900
I actually do like the idea more that if it was, like, guys, we're totally out of ideas.

00:50:24.140 --> 00:50:25.700
We really need help.

00:50:26.260 --> 00:50:27.440
They were in crunch.

00:50:27.740 --> 00:50:29.000
They were obviously in crunch.

00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:33.240
They make these games once a year and there's a team of, like, six people making them.

00:50:35.300 --> 00:50:36.940
It's almost like it's going to be harder.

00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:38.100
Where it's like, oh, yeah, we got to pick.

00:50:38.260 --> 00:50:41.540
Now we have to design things based off of something someone else came up with.

00:50:41.620 --> 00:50:43.180
We have to design, like, gameplay around it.

00:50:43.560 --> 00:50:56.320
But while we're talking about the design of these things, I do want to also just say I really, just all the enemies, everyone, everything on screen, like, in a regular stage, I just, I really like it.

00:50:56.320 --> 00:51:03.480
Like, they're so silly, but so cool and still kind of scary, like, at the same time.

00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:09.780
And it's just like it all, they should not, all three of those things shouldn't fit together so well, but they do.

00:51:10.380 --> 00:51:14.200
I really appreciate the design of all these Mega Man games.

00:51:14.660 --> 00:51:20.720
Yeah, at the very least, you can say that it's too many enemies on a screen or that the enemies are really hard or whatever.

00:51:20.720 --> 00:51:30.520
But, like, it is also, like, thoughtful enemy design in the sense of, like, how each enemy is completely different from each other.

00:51:30.760 --> 00:51:36.720
Yeah, it's not just, like, a different skin shade than every other enemy that you fought.

00:51:36.860 --> 00:51:38.720
And they just come at you and run at you.

00:51:39.160 --> 00:51:39.960
Exactly, yeah.

00:51:40.260 --> 00:51:44.940
They have mechanics. So the pole vaulting guy sucks, but it's also, like, really cleverly designed.

00:51:45.040 --> 00:51:56.320
Yeah. We were, you were talking about contests, Joe, and I just wanted to mention the two that I know of, which is, I think, Nintendo held it for Legend of Zelda Link to the Past.

00:51:56.720 --> 00:52:06.000
They're the winner of a contest, I think, in the power, maybe something else, was in, like, a secret house that you could get into.

00:52:06.000 --> 00:52:10.320
And his name would be in the game, so he was literally in The Legend of Zelda.

00:52:11.160 --> 00:52:13.600
And you know this one, but I'll tell the listeners.

00:52:13.800 --> 00:52:22.800
There's also the boss, the secret boss in Kingdom Hearts 1, Kurt Ziza, which sounds like a villain to begin with.

00:52:23.020 --> 00:52:27.980
Yes. Like, they couldn't have. And thank God the guy's name was Kurt Ziza and not, like, Jim Smith.

00:52:28.160 --> 00:52:30.540
