jump. Uh, even allowing Mega Man to jump out of pits and such like he can just jump almost the

01:08:05.580 --> 01:08:06.820
entire height of the screen.

01:08:06.820 --> 01:08:10.300
If you hold up, it will slow down the animations.

01:08:10.820 --> 01:08:16.700
And if you hold up and a, it will freeze the timer on some of the animations.

01:08:16.700 --> 01:08:21.120
So not like the, there's no like in game clock or whatever, but like the timing on some of

01:08:21.120 --> 01:08:29.880
the animations, including like no, yeah, enemy attacks and explosions and other things.

01:08:29.880 --> 01:08:35.480
Um, so it, it, it, it even causes like some bosses to just like freeze in place.

01:08:35.880 --> 01:08:39.940
So, um, if you, if you haven't tried that plug in a second controller.

01:08:40.420 --> 01:08:45.840
All right. That, that sounds like something that would happen to a game with a, uh, rough design schedule.

01:08:46.200 --> 01:08:51.780
Yeah. But again, like, would you ever think to plug in a second controller on a one player game?

01:08:52.420 --> 01:08:57.800
No. Should Mega Man three have had a battle mode where you, you and, uh, one of you plays as

01:08:57.800 --> 01:09:01.080
Mega Man, one of you plays as Proto Man and you have all the power ups and you just like

01:09:01.080 --> 01:09:02.800
shoot at each other in an, in an arena.

01:09:03.300 --> 01:09:06.520
No, that's kind of just what the Proto Man battles are.

01:09:06.660 --> 01:09:08.280
Right. I do love that.

01:09:08.280 --> 01:09:09.240
I think it is online.

01:09:10.900 --> 01:09:12.920
Like journey. You don't know you're online.

01:09:13.180 --> 01:09:15.680
Spoiler. I think I ever played it.

01:09:15.820 --> 01:09:17.080
Wow. Huge spoiler.

01:09:17.600 --> 01:09:19.180
Um, but probably not now.

01:09:19.340 --> 01:09:21.400
I mean, is anyone online playing journey right now?

01:09:21.480 --> 01:09:22.700
I'm just, it's like, to be fair.

01:09:22.900 --> 01:09:24.500
I never played it. So I'm just guessing.

01:09:24.720 --> 01:09:25.860
So it's really not a spoiler.

01:09:26.020 --> 01:09:27.020
It's a theory that I have.

01:09:27.160 --> 01:09:29.080
Well, we'll go on that journey together, Joe.

01:09:30.140 --> 01:09:31.760
I love it. You can't, you can't do that.

01:09:32.200 --> 01:09:36.600
The PlayStation one version of this game, which exists, apparently I had no idea.

01:09:37.040 --> 01:09:39.280
Um, it rock man complete works.

01:09:39.440 --> 01:09:45.060
So that makes me think it's a Japanese only, uh, game, but it added a, uh, what was called

01:09:45.060 --> 01:09:51.620
a Navi mode, I guess, navigational mode, uh, which added onscreen hint pop-ups.

01:09:52.140 --> 01:09:55.520
Um, which I can only imagine must be incredibly annoying.

01:09:56.500 --> 01:10:01.280
Yeah. Right. Like, like how, what could it have done other than been like, use this weapon on this boss,

01:10:01.420 --> 01:10:05.920
right? Like, like it's, there's not a lot of like, you know, Oh, watch your, watch your step.

01:10:06.140 --> 01:10:08.940
Right. Like you don't need something like that.

01:10:09.480 --> 01:10:14.360
Uh, but again, just another thing that from soft stole from earlier video games.

01:10:15.060 --> 01:10:19.540
And, uh, these, these features were added to the mega man anniversary collection.

01:10:19.540 --> 01:10:25.320
So maybe I should look at, um, playing like the, the baby mode, uh, with my copy.

01:10:25.340 --> 01:10:28.600
Yeah. I could use, I could definitely use a baby mode for these games.

01:10:28.600 --> 01:10:35.340
I feel like I also heard though, um, that there was like extreme lag on the anniversary

01:10:35.340 --> 01:10:36.460
collection on PS2.

01:10:36.600 --> 01:10:38.360
So maybe that's why I was so bad at those games.

01:10:38.660 --> 01:10:43.960
What could possibly make a PS2 game lag an NES game?

01:10:44.280 --> 01:10:46.700
I don't know what made a PS1 disc.

01:10:47.680 --> 01:10:50.260
Why did a PS1 disc make Chrono Trigger lag?

01:10:50.800 --> 01:10:53.300
Why did the chicken cross the road?

01:10:53.480 --> 01:10:55.000
Oh, actually, you know what? Yeah, Joe, you're right.

01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:57.480
It was the load times, not actual lagging.

01:10:57.720 --> 01:11:01.140
And also like, would it matter if things lagged in a turn-based game?

01:11:02.060 --> 01:11:07.300
Uh, anyway, um, it's some, some questions.

01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:15.300
Okay. Which single mechanic makes mega man three feel the most different from mega man two?

01:11:15.500 --> 01:11:21.340
The slide, the new friendly dog or the doc robot stages?

01:11:21.820 --> 01:11:27.440
The slide. Uh, see, I might, I might, uh, play devil's advocate here and say, uh, I think maybe the

01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:34.480
doc robot stages, the slide does, but I feel like honestly, it didn't, it having not played

01:11:34.480 --> 01:11:37.100
the other ones in a while, I was not like, oh my God, this is so different.

01:11:37.100 --> 01:11:41.460
I actually had to remember, but yeah, wait, was there a slide in mega man two or not?

01:11:41.460 --> 01:11:46.640
So like, it definitely does make a difference, but I don't think it was like, uh, I don't

01:11:46.640 --> 01:11:51.720
think it was as significant as there being eight more bosses, you know, granted now just

01:11:51.720 --> 01:11:53.820
to argue with myself here, you don't even have to talk.

01:11:53.940 --> 01:11:54.760
I'll just argue with myself.

01:11:55.300 --> 01:12:02.480
Um, granted that the fact that they are taking previous bosses, maybe just by definition

01:12:02.480 --> 01:12:06.600
makes it more like the previous games and not more, uh, separate.

01:12:06.820 --> 01:12:07.860
So who knows?

01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:15.160
I mean, my argument against that is that, uh, some people would never even notice that they're,

01:12:15.260 --> 01:12:18.660
that those bosses exist because they don't get to them.

01:12:18.920 --> 01:12:22.060
They don't get to them, uh, which is, uh, me.

01:12:22.060 --> 01:12:29.580
Um, but, uh, so I'm gonna, I'm gonna stick with the, I'm gonna stick with the slide to

01:12:29.580 --> 01:12:33.560
me. It's like, you know, like you, you can obviously, you can automatically tell the difference

01:12:33.560 --> 01:12:41.240
between, uh, between like Tony Hawk pro skater two and Tony Hawk pro skater three, because

01:12:41.240 --> 01:12:44.440
in Tony Hawk pro skater three, you had the revert.

01:12:45.280 --> 01:12:51.280
And that means you could like, you could have these really crazy long, like combos going.

01:12:51.280 --> 01:12:52.960
And I could be wrong.

01:12:52.980 --> 01:13:00.580
And maybe that was into, but, uh, but like it, it's something foundational and like that

01:13:00.580 --> 01:13:04.920
slide is like a foundational move that you're going to either use all the time or completely

01:13:04.920 --> 01:13:08.080
forget about, but it's still like, it's a part of your move set.

01:13:08.380 --> 01:13:09.760
Yeah. I'm, I'm sold.

01:13:10.040 --> 01:13:11.080
I, I rescind.

01:13:21.280 --> 01:13:22.320
Sorry.

01:13:55.600 --> 01:14:02.820
What one change would you make in a Mega Man 3 remaster without losing the NES feel?

01:14:03.160 --> 01:14:07.420
Hmm. I might make my Proto Man change.

01:14:07.620 --> 01:14:11.340
Give him some power-ups of his own.

01:14:11.660 --> 01:14:16.300
Should he have new power-ups you've never seen, or should he have callback power-ups?

01:14:16.360 --> 01:14:17.380
What are you thinking?

01:14:17.380 --> 01:14:26.700
I like new power-ups you've never seen, only because I like the idea of there being these unobtainable things that he's doing.

01:14:26.800 --> 01:14:28.900
He's on his own alternate journey.

01:14:28.900 --> 01:14:30.540
He's an alternate version of you.

01:14:30.600 --> 01:14:31.740
He's got totally different things.

01:14:32.100 --> 01:14:43.220
Maybe if you really want to make the game development a little more complicated, give him one power-up that counters each of your power-ups in some way.

01:14:43.220 --> 01:14:51.660
It's kind of interesting that we've never had a Final Fantasy game where halfway through we run into the other group that's questing to take down...

01:14:51.660 --> 01:14:54.100
Yeah, we had the same plan over in our town.

01:14:54.420 --> 01:14:56.680
We defeated this boss already.

01:14:56.820 --> 01:14:57.840
We're planning to do this.

01:14:57.940 --> 01:14:59.660
It's like, oh, you guys want to team up?

01:15:00.360 --> 01:15:02.820
And they're like, no, we want to stop you, too.

01:15:03.960 --> 01:15:05.940
There's got to be a Final Fantasy that has that.

01:15:06.160 --> 01:15:12.060
Maybe not a Final Fantasy, but definitely an RPG has to have that mechanic in it somewhere.

01:15:12.220 --> 01:15:13.820
Because that's just really fun. That's a fun idea.

01:15:13.980 --> 01:15:14.800
I agree with you.

01:15:14.880 --> 01:15:15.960
I like the Proto Man one.

01:15:16.280 --> 01:15:18.160
Sean, not to put you on the spot, but can you top it?

01:15:18.980 --> 01:15:20.640
No, I don't have any.

01:15:21.080 --> 01:15:25.980
I think it would be a multitude of changes.

01:15:26.600 --> 01:15:27.660
Yeah, I hear you.

01:15:27.720 --> 01:15:35.800
I hear you. But also, I feel like you did call out your biggest complaint was about the ammunition not replenishing between deaths.

01:15:35.840 --> 01:15:40.540
And maybe that's a simple enough fix to slap a remaster on it.

01:15:41.040 --> 01:15:42.140
It's now easier.

01:15:43.120 --> 01:15:43.940
There you go.

01:15:44.640 --> 01:15:48.300
Yeah, and I didn't think about the question either, if I'm being honest.

01:15:48.300 --> 01:15:56.400
But in terms of what I would want to see now while still keeping the NES feel, I think you can just release the same game.

01:15:56.400 --> 01:16:02.720
But let's give these games the pixel remaster treatment where you can kind of tweak them as necessary.

01:16:02.940 --> 01:16:08.040
Like, okay, enemies do 0.5 times damage now.

01:16:08.100 --> 01:16:12.120
And you just turn that setting on and you go through the game and you're able to experience it.

01:16:12.240 --> 01:16:14.280
But it's kind of like, you know what you did.

01:16:14.420 --> 01:16:16.840
You went into the settings and you had to change those things.

01:16:16.840 --> 01:16:18.640
There's no, like, easy mode.

01:16:18.900 --> 01:16:21.040
But you have to live with that.

01:16:21.240 --> 01:16:27.160
It's the same thing with turning experience points up four times on any of the Final Fantasy pixel remasters.

01:16:27.400 --> 01:16:32.960
I'm going to be able to sleep at night doing that because I have now gained enough time to go to sleep.

01:16:33.120 --> 01:16:39.140
If I did the one-time experience, I would be still playing to make up the same amount of time as the four times.

01:16:39.200 --> 01:16:44.660
So I'm fine with it. I think a lot of games, not even just NES games, but a lot of older games,

01:16:44.660 --> 01:16:50.960
could benefit from just, like, this settings menu where you kind of, like, adjust the feel of, like,

01:16:51.720 --> 01:16:55.220
especially for JRPGs, how often turn-based encounters happen.

01:16:55.380 --> 01:16:56.560
Do they happen at all?

01:16:56.760 --> 01:17:01.060
Like, you know, I'm not saying change the system where, like, it scales with you or something.

01:17:01.200 --> 01:17:02.480
God, no. Please don't do that.

01:17:02.740 --> 01:17:04.540
I have one now.

01:17:04.840 --> 01:17:06.840
Please. Blood and gore.

01:17:07.300 --> 01:17:08.900
Why not? It's Mega Man.

01:17:08.900 --> 01:17:11.680
Yeah, have, like, a blood and gore slider.

01:17:12.320 --> 01:17:18.900
You can go from, like, none, like, default, and then, like, truly, like, gib-tastic, like,

01:17:19.340 --> 01:17:23.780
super meat boy stuff on all the walls and stuff.

01:17:23.980 --> 01:17:25.600
Would it be blood or would it be oil?

01:17:26.000 --> 01:17:26.960
Oh, you're right.

01:17:27.280 --> 01:17:28.720
It's like oil and gore.

01:17:29.840 --> 01:17:35.600
I think that you should still keep the graphics just pixelated, you know,

01:17:35.600 --> 01:17:42.620
exactly the same graphics but have, like, fully, like, Unreal Engine 5 blood and gore coming out of it.

01:17:42.620 --> 01:17:47.900
Yeah, I'm going to do it. The Japanese subtitle of Mega Man 3 was Dr.

01:17:48.100 --> 01:17:51.300
Wily no Saigo, which means the end of Dr.

01:17:51.460 --> 01:17:57.300
Wily. So I guess they were trying to, like, fake out a trilogy here, but I don't think anyone thought

01:17:57.300 --> 01:17:59.340
that this was, like, the end of a trilogy.

01:17:59.340 --> 01:18:03.700
But you could make the case that, like, Mega Man 1, Dr.

01:18:03.820 --> 01:18:05.520
Light and Dr. Wily are working together,

01:18:05.520 --> 01:18:07.280
and Dr. Wily betrays Dr.

01:18:07.440 --> 01:18:09.100
Light, and then you have that.

01:18:09.540 --> 01:18:12.440
In Mega Man 2, now Wily's acting on his own.

01:18:12.820 --> 01:18:17.320
So, you know, you've got to take him down with the new robots he created without the help of Dr.

01:18:17.440 --> 01:18:26.140
Light. And now, at the end of the trilogy, Wily's back with Light, but only to betray him again.

01:18:26.140 --> 01:18:29.500
But that's not really, like, I don't know, that's just, like, a repeat of the story of one a little bit,

01:18:29.540 --> 01:18:31.780
except for now you already know that he did the betraying.

01:18:32.120 --> 01:18:34.560
Yeah, that sounds a little, like, daytime TV.

01:18:35.680 --> 01:18:39.560
Maybe that's exactly what Mega Man was made for, a little telenovela.

01:18:41.300 --> 01:18:43.180
It's a will they, won't they with Dr.

01:18:43.260 --> 01:18:44.260
Light and Dr. Wily.

01:18:44.420 --> 01:18:45.700
Will they get back together?

01:18:45.700 --> 01:18:56.180
Yeah, they should have, like, between each level had sort of, like, a B plot that went over, like, their little love affair.

01:18:56.440 --> 01:18:59.560
Yeah, just seeing them, like, out to dinner, and, you know, Dr.

01:18:59.680 --> 01:19:03.880
Wily's like, what do you say we play credit card roulette to decide who pays for the bill?

01:19:06.900 --> 01:19:08.820
Do they have credit cards in Mega Man?

01:19:08.980 --> 01:19:10.340
I don't think there's money.

01:19:10.720 --> 01:19:11.920
Yeah, there's no money either.

01:19:11.980 --> 01:19:14.580
That's so interesting. There's three things, that's it.

01:19:16.940 --> 01:19:20.360
Robots, people, and robot dogs.

01:19:21.380 --> 01:19:25.660
Yes. But that begs the question, are there dogs in the Mega Man world?

01:19:25.900 --> 01:19:27.140
No. Just robot dogs?

01:19:27.300 --> 01:19:28.140
Yeah. Yep.

01:19:28.500 --> 01:19:30.040
Maybe they're in, like, a simulation.

01:19:30.280 --> 01:19:31.540
Maybe Dr. Light and Dr.

01:19:31.620 --> 01:19:33.540
Wily went inside a computer.

01:19:33.640 --> 01:19:35.600
Well, yes, of course they are, right?

01:19:36.820 --> 01:19:39.940
Is it a simulation, though, or, like, just inside of a program?

01:19:40.420 --> 01:19:42.260
Well, we are in a simulation, so.

01:19:42.260 --> 01:19:43.500
And they're in our program.

01:19:43.540 --> 01:19:45.080
Right. They're in a simulation. Got it.

01:19:45.900 --> 01:19:48.020
Okay, that's all my stuff.

01:19:48.020 --> 01:19:51.700
I just wanted to mention real fast, since I was talking about the anniversary collection.

01:19:51.700 --> 01:19:58.400
There is one other way to, like, play these in the old-fashioned way, and that is with

01:19:58.400 --> 01:20:02.580
the Sega Genesis release of The Wily Wars.

01:20:02.580 --> 01:20:03.520
The Wily Wars.

01:20:03.520 --> 01:20:05.160
It only came out on Genesis.

01:20:06.040 --> 01:20:06.840
The Wily Wars?

01:20:07.120 --> 01:20:08.280
Yeah, The Wily Wars.

01:20:08.420 --> 01:20:13.320
And it remakes Mega Man's 1, 2, and 3 with a 16-bit art style.

01:20:13.960 --> 01:20:18.160
But apparently, also, like, some different physics and stuff, too.

01:20:18.340 --> 01:20:19.280
So, I'm curious.

01:20:19.320 --> 01:20:21.820
Like, are The Wily Wars, like, panned?

01:20:21.940 --> 01:20:23.740
Like, do they not feel like Mega Man?

01:20:23.840 --> 01:20:28.260
Or is it, like, a slept-on thing where it's like, oh, a lot of people just don't know about

01:20:28.260 --> 01:20:32.960
it? And turns out, like, that, like, just like how Super Mario All-Stars doesn't, like, replace

01:20:33.380 --> 01:20:34.180
Super Mario Bros.

01:20:34.240 --> 01:20:35.420
1, 2, and 3 on the NES.

01:20:35.680 --> 01:20:39.840
It kind of, like, is like, well, I prefer to play it on Super Nintendo with All-Stars.

01:20:39.860 --> 01:20:43.720
Or, no, I prefer to play it on the NES, like, the way it was intended.

01:20:44.320 --> 01:20:47.620
Interesting conversation. I don't have an opinion, because I've never played Wily Wars.

01:20:48.420 --> 01:20:51.200
But I do have an opinion on something, Sean.

01:20:52.080 --> 01:20:58.680
And that is if Mega Man 3 will be on the Essential Games list.

01:21:02.780 --> 01:21:07.660
For me, Mega Man 3 is the tightest Mega Man yet.

01:21:08.080 --> 01:21:19.000
Mega Man 2, while a great game, Mega Man 3 felt more accessible, more dynamic, and the

01:21:19.000 --> 01:21:28.660
new mechanics that were added, the slide, Rush, and the Doc Robot stages, are all, like,

01:21:28.880 --> 01:21:33.920
even if I don't love the length of the Doc Robot stages, they're all, like, welcome things

01:21:33.920 --> 01:21:35.980
in terms of expanding Mega Man.

01:21:36.060 --> 01:21:37.940
They all make it feel like a bigger game.

01:21:38.680 --> 01:21:44.640
I don't feel like this game is unfinished or, like, a decline in the series.

01:21:44.800 --> 01:21:47.440
I feel like the slide isn't just, like, a gimmick thing.

01:21:47.440 --> 01:21:52.340
It feels like it's part of Mega Man, which makes it, like I said, it will be interesting

01:21:52.340 --> 01:21:53.900
to go back to 1 or 2.

01:21:54.320 --> 01:22:04.320
And I know I said it on Mega Man 2's episode, but now I really question both 1 and 2 being

01:22:04.320 --> 01:22:09.880
on the Essential Games list, and especially 1, obviously, when 3 can get the job done.

01:22:09.880 --> 01:22:18.160
1. I think it will just be about, though, like, Mega Man 3 and 2 are kind of, like, the same

01:22:18.160 --> 01:22:21.620
exact engine, the same game, so they're almost, like, complements to each other.

01:22:21.940 --> 01:22:25.540
Do you just have to, like, suck it up and put 1?

01:22:25.660 --> 01:22:28.160
Like, are we in a situation where we need to do that?

01:22:28.180 --> 01:22:30.080
Or can we just agree that, like, both are great?

01:22:30.240 --> 01:22:31.700
Like, that's a discussion we'll have later.

01:22:31.700 --> 01:22:37.640
Today is all about Mega Man 3, and I'm happy to say that even though I think this game is

01:22:37.640 --> 01:22:46.400
still just as hard, the accessibility features that they added and just the kind of, like,

01:22:46.880 --> 01:22:53.680
the way that it flows as you move on, not becoming, like, this increasingly more challenging

01:22:53.680 --> 01:22:57.420
thing, but just kind of this thing that, like, well, if you made it this far, you can probably

01:22:57.420 --> 01:23:02.180
persevere feels better than what was happening with Mega Man 1 and 2, where it was like,

01:23:02.540 --> 01:23:05.100
yeah, you're lucky to be here, and you'll be lucky to get any further.

01:23:05.400 --> 01:23:10.780
I appreciated this change of pace in Mega Man 3, and so I'm giving it my Essential Games

01:23:10.780 --> 01:23:12.760
List stamp. What about you, Joe?

01:23:14.040 --> 01:23:18.480
I think that the Mega Man series, just talking about all three of them right now, they're still

01:23:18.480 --> 01:23:22.200
the goat when it comes to power-ups.

01:23:22.200 --> 01:23:27.800
Just their ability to keep things balanced in a way where, like, everything that you get

01:23:27.800 --> 01:23:28.640
is useful.

01:23:28.900 --> 01:23:30.980
You get tons of power-ups.

01:23:31.120 --> 01:23:36.800
They're all very, well, mostly very helpful, very useful in different scenarios, but you

01:23:36.800 --> 01:23:38.420
never feel overpowered.

01:23:38.480 --> 01:23:46.260
It still feels like a challenge in that, like, there are specific things that are being balanced.

01:23:46.440 --> 01:23:50.660
There's bosses and enemies that are being balanced where you can beat it without these things

01:23:50.660 --> 01:23:51.660
or with them.

01:23:51.820 --> 01:23:57.880
Like, that's quite the feat, in my opinion, to design something like that.

01:23:58.360 --> 01:24:03.440
I feel like this episode, we have sounded maybe a little negative.

01:24:03.780 --> 01:24:10.020
I'll be honest, I thought that, Mike, I thought you were not going to vote at Essential, just

01:24:10.020 --> 01:24:12.040
based on the episode so far.

01:24:12.640 --> 01:24:17.780
I thought that, and maybe, you know, Sean will have a chance to prove this right or wrong

01:24:17.780 --> 01:24:22.000
on his episode, but I thought I was going to be a lone Essential vote for this one.

01:24:22.320 --> 01:24:24.240
But I really did enjoy it.

01:24:24.880 --> 01:24:27.740
I haven't played the other two in a long time.

01:24:29.140 --> 01:24:34.620
So in my flawed memories of two, I guess I vaguely remember maybe liking two a little

01:24:34.620 --> 01:24:44.480
more, but I do firmly believe that, like, there's no need for, like, only one game existing

01:24:44.480 --> 01:24:47.620
on this, you know, in this series existing on the Essential Games list.

01:24:47.720 --> 01:24:52.620
I think that if all three games are fantastic games that are worth playing, then all three

01:24:52.620 --> 01:24:54.040
games are Essential Games.

01:24:54.040 --> 01:25:00.260
So what I'm bringing it down to is, like, if somebody asks me, hey, I'm into video games,

01:25:00.400 --> 01:25:01.740
should I play Mega Man 3?

01:25:02.600 --> 01:25:03.840
What is my answer going to be?

01:25:03.880 --> 01:25:10.460
My answer is going to be definitely for Mega Man 1, 2, and 3, at least before I do a revisit

01:25:10.460 --> 01:25:11.940
of them. That's where I stand for now.

01:25:12.100 --> 01:25:15.960
So right now, I still, I'm going to give my Essential vote for three different games.

01:25:15.960 --> 01:25:17.320
I think 1, 2, and 3 are essential.

01:25:18.220 --> 01:25:19.140
All right, Sean.

01:25:19.880 --> 01:25:29.060
Okay, yeah. So I, like, I mentioned earlier that I revisited our past, at least our Essential Games list

01:25:29.060 --> 01:25:36.440
sections for Mega Man 1 and 2, just so that I could recalibrate where my head has been

01:25:36.440 --> 01:25:37.980
these past hard for many years.

01:25:40.200 --> 01:25:44.100
And I think it's because, like, I don't know, I think my mood has just shifted.

01:25:44.100 --> 01:25:52.080
Like, I think I have less patience now, because I didn't really, I didn't have all that much

01:25:52.080 --> 01:25:53.160
fun playing this game.

01:25:54.460 --> 01:26:00.680
And I know that I did in 1 and 2, but does that mean, does that mean that, like, this

01:26:00.680 --> 01:26:05.500
isn't essential? Because, like, it's just not really my cup of tea right now?

01:26:05.640 --> 01:26:06.720
Because it really isn't.

01:26:08.780 --> 01:26:13.540
But, like, it's sort of like, you know, when I talk about football and, you know, there

01:26:13.540 --> 01:26:18.400
was a time in my life where I would have just said, like, you know, no, no, no, Tom Brady

01:26:18.400 --> 01:26:24.200
sucks. Tom Brady is a system QB, and it's all Bill Belichick.

01:26:24.500 --> 01:26:31.120
And, like, there's nothing that he's got that you couldn't plug anybody else in.

01:26:31.120 --> 01:26:33.160
And he'd win just as many Super Bowls.

01:26:33.860 --> 01:26:39.920
But, you know, looking back on stuff, and, you know, he then won another Super Bowl somewhere

01:26:39.920 --> 01:26:43.740
else, and then Bill Belichick wasn't very good.

01:26:43.740 --> 01:26:44.700
I'm getting off topic.

01:26:44.880 --> 01:26:52.040
Basically, it's more so, like, you have to visually, like, I visually see objectively that

01:26:52.040 --> 01:26:56.880
this is just an improvement on two games that I voted essential.

01:26:58.240 --> 01:27:01.220
That is, like, that is what this is.

01:27:02.020 --> 01:27:05.580
Like, there's no way that this is a worse game than those two.

01:27:06.500 --> 01:27:10.340
I just didn't, you know, I just, like, I'm at the point in, I'm at a point in time where

01:27:10.340 --> 01:27:12.080
it's just, I didn't really have that much fun with it.

01:27:12.280 --> 01:27:16.720
But, you know, as, like, an objective observer, I'm just going to say, yeah, it's essential.

01:27:18.420 --> 01:27:22.020
I'm concurring. Like, I'm not going to argue about it.

01:27:22.680 --> 01:27:27.040
I do think you bring up a good point, though, about one specific thing, and that is the

01:27:27.040 --> 01:27:32.820
enjoyment that you are having as somebody who is playing through all of these NES games

01:27:32.820 --> 01:27:36.320
with limited time, you know, like, we release an episode every Friday.

01:27:36.900 --> 01:27:43.280
Like, it's hard to, like, pick up a franchise that you last touched years ago, right?

01:27:43.400 --> 01:27:45.460
Like, Mega Man 2 was a while back now.

01:27:45.460 --> 01:27:50.820
And it's hard to also just, like, keep switching gears and being good at these things.

01:27:51.040 --> 01:27:56.660
And Mega Man games in general require them to, you have to be good at them to have fun.

01:27:56.780 --> 01:28:00.200
You are otherwise learning how to play the game.

01:28:00.960 --> 01:28:06.540
I think that's worth mentioning, that Mega Man 3 and Mega Man 2, and Mega Man 2 actually

01:28:06.540 --> 01:28:08.660
had, like, an easy mode, if you recall.

01:28:08.780 --> 01:28:12.380
It had, like, a, they called it normal mode, but you could also play difficult mode.

01:28:12.380 --> 01:28:15.520
So, that one even had, like, a toned down version thing.

01:28:15.800 --> 01:28:18.800
Mega Man 1 was the hardest of the batch, no question.

01:28:19.000 --> 01:28:24.060
But, like, even if these games become more accessible, that's from the viewpoint of, like,

01:28:24.720 --> 01:28:29.980
changing things within the design of Mega Man games to kind of, like, tone them down.

01:28:30.080 --> 01:28:31.560
They're still Mega Man games.

01:28:31.620 --> 01:28:38.700
They're still challenging. Compared to the games that we play nowadays where, like, basically everyone wins as long

01:28:38.700 --> 01:28:40.200
as they're willing to play, right?

01:28:40.200 --> 01:28:46.220
Like, I can't think of somebody who wouldn't be able to finish God of War 2018 if they just

01:28:46.220 --> 01:28:47.360
wanted to play it.

01:28:47.480 --> 01:28:51.260
Like, they're never going to get stuck in, like, that boss is too hard.

01:28:51.400 --> 01:28:53.120
Like, it's basically like watching a story.

01:28:53.600 --> 01:28:55.740
Mega Man is not that kind of series.

01:28:55.940 --> 01:29:02.380
And so, yeah, if you're, like, picking it up and going through it and dying a lot, like,

01:29:02.460 --> 01:29:06.420
Joe even joked in the episode that his Mega Man is the one that explodes all the time.

01:29:06.420 --> 01:29:11.780
Like, yeah, that happens, but that has to also be, like, a rewarding thing, too.

01:29:11.900 --> 01:29:17.800
And I think that's what Mega Man gets right is that, like, you'll die, I don't know, you

01:29:17.800 --> 01:29:19.460
know, 20, 30 times or whatever.

01:29:19.680 --> 01:29:21.600
But, like, you'll get better along the way.

01:29:21.740 --> 01:29:24.380
This isn't, there's no cheap shots in this game.

01:29:24.500 --> 01:29:28.900
There are things that might feel unavoidable or that you personally just can't overcome.

01:29:29.100 --> 01:29:30.800
For me, that happened to be Yellow Devil.

01:29:30.800 --> 01:29:36.700
But on an infinite timescale, like, everything on Mega Man is very achievable in the sense

01:29:36.700 --> 01:29:38.700
of, like, what NES games are offering.

01:29:38.860 --> 01:29:43.980
There are tons of really cheap or needlessly hard NES games.

01:29:43.980 --> 01:29:48.620
This is just one that requires more, like, patience to love.

01:29:48.940 --> 01:29:53.960
Yeah. I also, I was going to mention something similar when we were talking about the, um, kind of

01:29:53.960 --> 01:29:58.660
the artificially drawn-out length of the game, which I don't disagree with.

01:29:58.660 --> 01:30:03.300
I do think that, like, yeah, having the, the, those extra levels, but having them not

01:30:03.300 --> 01:30:05.980
be new levels does make it feel a little artificial.

01:30:05.980 --> 01:30:09.640
But it probably is an easier pill to swallow when you're playing this game.

01:30:09.780 --> 01:30:15.700
You're picking it up and putting it down over, like, years as a child, as opposed to us where

01:30:15.700 --> 01:30:19.000
we're, like, yeah, we got, we got six days to play.

01:30:19.080 --> 01:30:22.820
You know, obviously we start sometimes a little before the week before, but, like, still, it's,

01:30:22.880 --> 01:30:27.680
like, it's just a thing that's, there is a time limit where we're, like, we got to get

01:30:27.680 --> 01:30:31.240
as far as we can in this amount of time, as opposed to, like, yeah, if this is just the

01:30:31.240 --> 01:30:36.060
game that I had for the year, you know, one of my two or three video games, then it would

01:30:36.060 --> 01:30:39.340
be, like, yeah, this is how far I am, and, you know, I'm going to put it down for a few

01:30:39.340 --> 01:30:41.160
months. I'm going to pick it back up eventually, you know.

01:30:41.220 --> 01:30:48.120
And that's sort of, that's sort of my, it's, it's all, it's just also being kind of, like,

01:30:48.240 --> 01:30:49.640
trying to have some internal consistency.

01:30:49.640 --> 01:30:55.640
But, like, I know I have used the defense in a lot of games that we have talked about

01:30:55.640 --> 01:30:59.540
difficulty in a negative sense of just, like, well, if I actually had more time, this would

01:30:59.540 --> 01:31:09.500
be, like, I'd find this a lot more satisfying, and the word I am looking for eludes me, but

01:31:09.500 --> 01:31:15.980
fulfilling. Whereas, you know, it's just, the time crunch kind of takes the magic out of it sometimes,

01:31:16.080 --> 01:31:17.560
but I still like doing it.

01:31:17.560 --> 01:31:23.280
Yeah, and without spoiling it, I do know what the change is in Mega Man 4.

01:31:23.360 --> 01:31:24.380
Do you guys?

01:31:24.800 --> 01:31:26.280
No. I don't. Okay, cool.

01:31:26.420 --> 01:31:27.420
So, I won't spoil it here.

01:31:27.420 --> 01:31:30.320
Is it online, secretly? It's, yeah, it's always online.

01:31:30.660 --> 01:31:31.800
He's barefoot now.

01:31:32.420 --> 01:31:34.000
Oh, that would be a twist, right?

01:31:34.140 --> 01:31:36.760
He takes, he takes off the blaster.

01:31:36.980 --> 01:31:38.300
He just fights with his fists now.

01:31:40.220 --> 01:31:42.440
It's actually Samus underneath all the armor.

01:31:44.180 --> 01:31:48.760
Samus versus Mega Man is, like, something that people didn't really make a big deal out of

01:31:48.760 --> 01:31:51.640
on Smash Brothers when they finally were both in the same game, right?

01:31:51.760 --> 01:31:55.620
Like, I feel like Mega Man Mario wasn't really, like, Mario's got Sonic.

01:31:55.880 --> 01:31:59.140
Yeah. Mega Man should be going off against Samus, I suppose.

01:31:59.840 --> 01:32:03.460
Or Samus against Simon or whatever, right?

01:32:03.460 --> 01:32:08.360
Or who, who's, who'd they put in for, did they put in Simon or did they put in Trevor?

01:32:08.900 --> 01:32:10.560
I think it's Simon. Good.

01:32:10.760 --> 01:32:11.560
Okay, no, I can't remember.

01:32:11.800 --> 01:32:17.060
I was, it's weird is, is like, I played Smash for, like, the longest time, and somehow

01:32:17.060 --> 01:32:18.740
DLC ruined it for me.

01:32:18.860 --> 01:32:23.760
Like, I stopped playing when they started doing those season pass things, and now I can't

01:32:23.760 --> 01:32:29.700
remember, like, any of the 87 people that are in Smash Brothers other than Mario and Yoshi.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:32.160
Is that one soccer player in it now?

01:32:33.180 --> 01:32:34.760
Oh, Ronaldo?

01:32:35.140 --> 01:32:36.400
Yeah, Ronaldo, he's in it, right?

01:32:36.420 --> 01:32:40.560
Yeah, he's, he's, well, he's in Fortnite, and I heard that just the concept of Fortnite

01:32:40.560 --> 01:32:42.600
is going to be the next character in Smash Brothers.

01:32:44.240 --> 01:32:45.220
After Home Depot.

01:32:45.760 --> 01:32:49.080
Home Depot for Smash 7 confirmed.
